+# FBI serial 4082 and the Gronlund cassette and transcript trail
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. A newly recovered Commission scan identifies **265A-NY-280350-302-4082** as an interview report about the **Flight 93 Gronlund voicemail cassette**. The April working memo cites that same serial in both its Flight 93 and Flight 77 sections. A separately recovered transcript packet adds production and fax references. [NARA finding aid, Team 7 Boxes 12–13](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf#page=105) · [Exact sources and hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Where serial 4082 appears
+
+| Source | What the page shows |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Team 7 Box 12 item 428, physical p. 4 lines 1–5 and 14–31** | The production header pairs **M-INT-00009985** with **265A-NY-280350-302-4082** and names the voicemail recipient as interview subject. The FD-302 body describes contact at approximately **6:45 p.m.**, receipt of the cassette at **7:30 p.m.**, and handover at the Boston FBI office at approximately **9:20 p.m.** on September 11, 2001. The form shows transcription on September 12. These are reported custody events. |
+| **FBI Vault September interview release, physical p. 11, production footer 000000002** | The held release uses different redaction and production fields. The form and body match the cassette account, including **6:45 p.m.**, **7:30 p.m.** and **9:20 p.m.**, the Boston handover and the September 12 transcription field. The source comparison treats these as two reproductions of the report. [FBI release, p. 11](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=11) |
+| **April 8 Concordance working memo, Team 7 Box 21 item 267, physical p. 1 lines 37–43, p. 3 lines 12–14 and p. 7 lines 43–45** | The Flight 77 operator paragraph cites **4082** beside **22171**. The Flight 93 Gronlund entry also cites **4082**, alongside **4080**, **1123** and **25851**. The later Flight 77 row again cites **4082** beside **22170** and **22171** and carries **“No tape indicated.”** Preserve all three citations and their contexts. |
+
+The cited serial's recovered body concerns the Gronlund cassette. The reason it appears in the Flight 77 passages remains open. The earlier study's negative search was limited to Box 17 Flight 77 and Box 19. Item 428 supplies the body that search left unlocated. The separate **22170** relay report, **22171** receiving-operator report, and missing Flight 77 operator recording retain their own evidence requirements. [Earlier serial and chart review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/476ce62251ea2f2c929d5735e68ba32192bf8e8a/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-operator-bates-and-flight77-list-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Earlier cassette review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5c2a489db46eb230900d41b05f1710497e636965/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-recording-custody-relays-2026-11-02/README.md)
+
+## Gronlund transcript production and contrary accounts
+
+- **Team 7 Box 13 item 786, pp. 1–3.** P. 1 lines 15–23 marks the packet **Requests #35-13 / Packet #13 / Commission Copy**. P. 2 lines 1–11 reproduce a fax report showing **JUL-01**, **15:33–15:34**, and **file no. 394**. The final year digit is obscured on the reviewed scan. P. 2 line 19 and p. 3 line 1 identify the voicemail transcript. Their visible headings give **“1 minute 1 second.”** The embedded layout text differs at the start of the expression, including **Tlninute 1 second** on p. 3. The packet leaves the underlying audio, original send and receive acknowledgments, and cassette-to-transcript production link open.
+- **Item 428, pp. 1 and 6, and item 267 p. 3.** The September 14 FD-302 continuation at item 428 p. 6 lines 11–19 reports a message time of **either 9:51 or 9:54**. Its content description includes a claim about what the hijackers threatened. The April working memo separately relays a reported White House destination claim. The April 22 Commission MFR in item 428 p. 1 lines 25–43 says the recipient heard a voicemail and expressly disputes the relayed destination account. Keep the retellings and the recipient's later description together. The recording and clock alignment remain untested.
+- **Different recording inquiries.** The May 14 list asks for a Gronlund message and separately for the Flight 77 operator call. Packet #13 supplies a Gronlund transcript production lead. The reviewed sources leave the May 14 dispatch and any Flight 77 recording delivery unverified. [May 14 list, question 10](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ba199e4b0d56c529e7d68da6646d1ab4ca36795b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-january-presentation-and-may-doj-questions-2026-11-08/README.md)
+
+## Open records and verification scope
+
+- **TEL01–TEL02.** Find the Boston cassette receipt, evidence item and subsequent custody records, native transcript preparation record and original fax/send/receipt records for packet #13. Match the physical audio to the transcript and separately recover the source version or index behind the April memo's Flight 77 citations.
+- **TEL03–TEL04.** Obtain the native call and routing rows and event/clock definitions. Test the Flight 77 operator association independently of the 4082 reference. Locate the preceding sheet or delivery index for chart 212 and the response to the May 14 questions.
+
+Four new ZIP members passed the archive-validator, range, length, CRC-32 and SHA-256 checks. All **163 physical pages** were screened by text layer. Box 17 Flight 93 p. 68 had blank extractable text. The Box 13 call-notes and Box 17 Flight 93 packet text screen returned no literal **4082** or **Flight Chart for Flight 77** hit. Selected header, body, timeline, citation and transcript-label regions were checked on renders. The held Vault PDF and working memo matched their stored hashes. The first text assertion stopped on the p. 3 transcript OCR variant, which is preserved separately from the visual reading. These checks concern documents and provenance. No audio playback, historical call test or caller-to-switch-event join was performed. [Source pins and test results](SOURCE-PINS.json)
